  "description": "Moog Taurus 3 analog bass pedal synthesizer: the MIDI CC table of its manual.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "Taurus 3 User's Manual",
      "notes": "MIDI CC table (pages 49, 50, 51) read by tools/profiles/moog/read-moog-pdf.mjs from Taurus_3_Manual.pdf (sha256 88006cf741660b63be1d2c8be3a9a8bafcbb3378166cd0cf918e1783415e52be), https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/Moog/BackOffice/Taurus_3_Manual.pdf. Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/moog/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/moog/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the manual's MIDI tables, with its printed name. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
    "No identity check: the manual prints no Device Inquiry reply.",
    "17 knob(s) are 14-bit, 0 - 16383: the MSB and the LSB the table prints, sent in that order: B FREQ (CC 10, LSB 42); BEAT (CC 11, LSB 43); GLIDE (CC 5, LSB 37); MIX (CC 15, LSB 47); ATTACK (CC 28, LSB 60); SUSTAIN (CC 30, LSB 62); DECAY (CC 29, LSB 61); LFO RATE/CLOCK (CC 3, LSB 35); FILTER (CC 6, LSB 38); PITCH (CC 8, LSB 40); MODWHEEL (CC 1, LSB 33); AMOUNT (CC 27, LSB 59); ATTACK (CC 23, LSB 55); DECAY (CC 24, LSB 56); CUTOFF (CC 19, LSB 51); RESONANCE (CC 21, LSB 53); ARP RATE (CC 4, LSB 36).",
    "Left out, printed without a controller (a panel switch, or `Varies`): CONTROL (CC Varies), MASTER (CC -), PRESET (CC -), CURSOR (CC -), STORE (CC -)."
  ],
